   "c": 3000,
   "cpp": 3000,
   "csharp": 3000,
   "fortran": 500
  },
  "max_size_kb": 800000
 },
 "selection_note": "created:<2021-01-01 is load-bearing. The corpus is the human-written baseline against which AI-assisted code is compared, and today's most-starred repositories include projects begun well into the LLM era \u2014 using those would answer the question before measuring it. The star bar is per language because 3,000 stars is not the same statement in every ecosystem: Fortran has zero repositories above it, so a single threshold would have excluded the language rather than measured it. The existing 40 rows are unchanged and still pinned to the commits they were measured at, so this change adds languages without re-rolling the original three. One C++ member was replaced after selection: CPlusPlusThings is a teaching repository, and the marker list gained \"things\" to exclude that category mechanically rather than by veto. It was found by its measurements (declarations 0.0078 against a 0.1005 reference) rather than by its name, which is the outcome-triggered discovery a mechanical corpus exists to prevent, so it is recorded here. Re-running selection with the new marker changed exactly one member: googletest took its place.",
